  "documented_limitations": [
    "The commissioning prompt referenced a switch cross_line_dec_allocation_permitted=false as an expected repository state; the switch does not exist anywhere in the repository or its history (mechanically searched over all commits). It was treated as an unverified prompt claim: no switch was invented and cross-line allocation semantics remain carried by the per-event origin_line fields alone.",
    "The register tool test had pinned first-unused claims (DEC-056, DEC-D18) against the moving HEAD; they went stale the moment the register legitimately grew. Corrected beside, not rewritten: the pins now bind to the immutable b0g start commit 537f9c2b0dbc0fefcda071deaa3de0df2f59655c and HEAD is checked structurally (gap-free, first-unused follows the maximum).",
    "The b0f blind/sample evidence checks are not inherited into the b0g manifest: they bind to the b0f commit pair by construction and can pass on no later commit. The durable b0f baseline and method checks carry forward.",
    "DEC-067's ordering half (the normative/determinative commit separation) is declared per block in the commit plans and consumed by no checker; the enforcement gap is documented in the DEC document itself.",
    "The alias binding R1..R10 to rule texts rests on the documented inference in each DEC document's Herkunft section; DEC-067's title is the B0g-authored reading label of an owner decision whose halves are lifted verbatim."
  ],
